{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Tonight I'm alone [D]without you my [A]dear
Its [A]seems there's a longing for you [E]still
[A]All I have to do now is [D]sit alone and [A]cry
In our [A]little cabin [E]home on the [A]hill
Oh [D]someone has taken you [A]from me
And [A]left me here all [E]alone
Just [A]listen to the rain [D]beyond my window [A]pane
In our [A]little cabin [E]home on the [A]hill
I hope you are happy tonight as you are
For in my heart there's a longing for you still
I'll just keep it there so I won't be alone
In our little cabin home on the hill
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And when you have come to the end of your way
And find there's no more happiness for you
Just let your thoughts turn back once more if you will
To our little cabin home on the hill
{end_of_chorus}
